{
  "dom_id": "step-e1100",
  "name": "Example: Determining the Finite Domain of a Function From Its Graph",
  "problem": "What is the domain of the function shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192268/assets/16ee469ac79597e3afc65844e27a156fd45d8cbd3234f2fdc74e0ab9b4554237.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The function above is defined for values between $x=-2$ and $x=2.$\n\n- Since there is a closed circle at $x=-2,$ this point is included in the domain.\n\n- Since there is a closed circle at $x=2,$ this point is also included in the domain.\n\nTherefore, the domain of this function is\n\n$$\n-2 \\leq x \\leq 2.\n$$\n\nUsing interval notation, we can write this as\n\n$$\nx \\in [-2,2].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e1100\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Determining the Finite Domain of a Function From Its Graph</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e1100\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <p>What is the domain of the function shown below?</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-05f0d4625d3290f29ec60fcc291e7cc4\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/05f0d4625d3290f29ec60fcc291e7cc4\"></div>\n                    </div>     \n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n              